  "name": "Sync Asana task changes to Google Calendar events",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "4c312c97-9857-4213-8836-5d45ea3b6bfa",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -720,
        -736
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 4,
        "width": 608,
        "height": 928,
        "content": "## Sync Asana task changes to Google Calendar events\n\nWho's it for: teams that create Asana tasks from Google Calendar events and want edits made in Asana to flow back to the calendar. This is the companion to the \"Sync Google Calendar events to Asana tasks\" template, which creates the tasks and the sync log this workflow relies on.\n\n### How it works\n1. An Asana trigger fires when a task in your project changes.\n2. The workflow finds the task's row in the sync log and skips changes it has already synced.\n3. It loads the task, its followers and assignee, and the linked calendar event, then compares them.\n4. For each difference it updates the calendar event: title, description, attendees, or start and end time.\n5. The task's last modified time is saved to the sync log.\n\n### Setup\n1. Use the same data table as the companion workflow (columns CalendarEventID, AsanaTaskID, LastSyncedUpdate) and select it in both Data Table nodes.\n2. In the Asana trigger, choose your workspace and the project the companion workflow creates tasks in.\n3. Fill in the Set configuration node: calendar ID and company email domain.\n4. Connect your Asana and Google Calendar accounts, then activate.\n\n### Customization\nRemove any branch after Route by detected change if you don't want that field synced back."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
